r-level ore shipments of about 25 tons each","evidence_id":"co-vermont-b478-p67","measurements":[{"commodity":"Ag","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":84.53},{"commodity":"Pb","unit":"percent","value":27.96}],"page_cite":"p. 67","page_text_sha256":"5112d7cc228283873889880cc224f5a7761ccd10c3e9754f34d9cd5ba0e5eb42","quote_verbatim":true,"source_id":"b478","verbatim_quote":"Eighty-five shipments of ore of about 25 tons each from the upper levels of the Vermont mine averaged 84.53 ounces silver and 27.96 per cent lead, or approximately $44.80 silver and $12.06 lead, a total gross value of $52.86 per ton","years":"historic shipments reported in 1911"}],"mine_id":"co-vermont","name":"Vermont mine"},{"county":"Hinsdale","district":"Lake City","evidence":[{"basis":"Small-mill concentrates from hand-sorted ore","evidence_id":"co-gallic-vulcan-b478-p73","measurements":[{"commodity":"Au","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":0.21},{"commodity":"Ag","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":10},{"commodity":"Pb","unit":"percent","value":50}],"page_cite":"p. 73","page_text_sha256":"41f0e769357b7e8b576029848138ebf9e3d397823cc17b220af2cb2d81739bcd","quote_verbatim":true,"source_id":"b478","verbatim_quote":"The total production of the Gallic and Vulcan mines is small. The ore treated has been hand sorted so that no general average of the run-of-mine ore can be obtained. The concentrates produced by a small mill installed on the ground are said to have contained about 0.21 ounce gold, 10 ounces silver, 50 per cent lead, and some zinc and iron.","years":"1911 report"}],"mine_id":"co-gallic-vulcan","name":"Gallic-Vulcan mines"},{"county":"Hinsdale","district":"Lake City","evidence":[{"basis":"Exceptional high-grade ore bunch at the main tunnel","evidence_id":"co-golden-fleece-b478-p106","measurements":[{"commodity":"Au","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":125},{"commodity":"Ag","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":1255}],"page_cite":"p. 106","page_text_sha256":"421b2e6cc5e670003c8da5f8cfecb9e84f546fdca0b07ae83774b17da5fd7eab","quote_verbatim":true,"source_id":"b478","verbatim_quote":"A few bunches of high-grade ore were found down as far as the main tunnel, where one bunch gave the phenomenal assay of 125 ounces gold and 1,255 ounces of silver.","years":"before 1911"}],"mine_id":"co-golden-fleece","name":"Golden Fleece mine"},{"county":"Hinsdale","district":"Lake City","evidence":[{"basis":"Superintendent-reported average yield of upper ore","evidence_id":"co-black-crook-b478-p116","measurements":[{"commodity":"Au","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":3},{"commodity":"Ag","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":21}],"page_cite":"p. 116","page_text_sha256":"17fb329b7aed2bea311fb4c4686fac1d89b8446a048c05ef9c7a8e31411d26de","quote_verbatim":true,"source_id":"b478","verbatim_quote":"Statements of the superintendent put the average yield of this upper ore at 21 ounces silver and 3 ounces gold.","years":"1884-era upper workings"}],"mine_id":"co-black-crook","name":"Black Crook mine"},{"county":"Hinsdale","district":"Lake City","evidence":[{"basis":"Reported average yield of lower-grade upper-level ore; exact single-valued copper term only","evidence_id":"co-moro-b478-p120","measurements":[{"commodity":"Cu","unit":"percent","value":4.4}],"page_cite":"p. 120","page_text_sha256":"b9e9ba73da83a0b387ee27b57a5da8250a6deb3b635991fe39aadc113e0b88da","quote_verbatim":true,"source_id":"b478","verbatim_quote":"The average yield of the lower-grade ore from the upper levels is stated to have been 10 to 17 ounces silver, 10 to 15 per cent lead, 4.4 per cent copper, and 6 to 15 per cent zinc, giving a total average value of $30 a ton.","years":"before 1911"}],"mine_id":"co-moro","name":"Moro mine"}],"schema_version":1,"sources":[{"authority":"U.S. Geological Survey","citation":"Irving, J. D., and Bancroft, Howland, 1911, USGS Bulletin 478.","document_sha256":"9b56597c64580e57cd35a5d293f8fbce55fe598badb45ed19fbcfd8b6fa93997","page_i